[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Merak Plan User Simulation\n\nFive realistic ambiguous engineering tasks.\nEach session simulates a user answer path, then scores the resulting plan.\nPass requires 10/10 per session, including tool choice, confidence gaps, and adaptation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[2.8, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Ops dashboard triage\n\nuser role: Support lead trying to clear stuck task executions before standup.\nuser prompt: The task execution dashboard is noisy. Make it easier to scan without turning it into a\nmarketing page.\nquestion type: recommended choice\nscore target: 10/10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[5.6, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Ops dashboard triage - questions\n\n1. target user: Who is the primary operator for the dense dashboard?\n   user: Support leads who triage failed and stale executions during daily ops.\n2. primary workflow: Which workflow should the first pass optimize?\n   user: Spot failed or stale runs, compare owner/status/age, then jump into the run.\n3. visual evidence: What proof should count before implementation starts?\n   user: Before/after screenshots at desktop and mobile widths plus one focused Playwright check.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[8.4, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Ops dashboard triage - plan proof\n\nscenario: ui-work\nscore: 10/10\ntools: read_repo_instructions, git_status, ripgrep, read_files, browser_qa, targeted_tests,\nno_mutation_in_plan_mode\nsuccess: Support leads can identify stale or failed runs within 10 seconds in the screenshot review.\ncounter: No table row, toolbar, or action text wraps or overlaps at mobile width.\nevidence: screenshots\nscope in: dashboard density and hierarchy, existing design primitives, desktop and mobile screenshot\nevidence\nscope out: new dashboard information architecture, decorative landing-page style redesign\nunknowns: existing design primitives, current viewport behavior\nconfidence gaps: design primitive ownership, viewport evidence\nsummary review: Plan is approved around support-lead triage, screenshot proof, and no broad redesign.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[11.2, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Persisted review status field\n\nuser role: Backend owner adding an API-visible task execution review field.\nuser prompt: Add review status to task executions and make sure API clients can read it.\nquestion type: freeform answer\nscore target: 10/10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[14.0, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Persisted review status field - questions\n\n1. field contract: What exact external API contract should the new field expose?\n   user: Expose review_status as nullable enum pending, approved, rejected.\n2. compatibility risk: How much compatibility ceremony do you want for existing rows?\n   user: No migration theater; existing rows can be null, but response schemas must type it explicitly.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[16.8, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Persisted review status field - plan proof\n\nscenario: backend-work\nscore: 10/10\ntools: read_repo_instructions, git_status, ripgrep, read_files, targeted_tests, migration_cycle,\nno_mutation_in_plan_mode\nsuccess: Task execution create/read/list endpoints return typed review_status for new and existing rows.\ncounter: Existing task execution API tests stay green and the migration remains reversible.\nevidence: pytest output\nscope in: data model column, schema response type, targeted API and service tests\nscope out: task review UI, historical backfill beyond nullable default\nunknowns: schema owner, existing migration pattern\nconfidence gaps: schema owner, migration reversibility\nsummary review: Plan is approved around nullable enum review_status and reversible migration evidence.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[19.6, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging remote dev boot failure\n\nuser role: Infra engineer debugging intermittent staging remote-dev session boot failures.\nuser prompt: Remote dev sessions in staging randomly do not boot. Figure out what is wrong.\nquestion type: multi-question flow\nscore target: 10/10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[22.4, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging remote dev boot failure - questions\n\n1. staging blast radius: What staging surface can this investigation touch?\n   user: Only staging remote-dev session startup; do not alter unrelated Temporal or API services.\n2. credential availability: Do you have cloud credentials available for direct checks?\n   user: Yes, AWS staging admin is available, but every cloud read/write should be explicit.\n3. rollback: What rollback proof should be part of the plan?\n   user: Capture current deploy commit and task definition before proposing any rollout.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[25.2, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging remote dev boot failure - plan proof\n\nscenario: infra-work\nscore: 10/10\ntools: read_repo_instructions, git_status, ripgrep, aws_staging, targeted_tests, github_checks,\nno_mutation_in_plan_mode\nsuccess: A staging health check shows remote-dev boot succeeds on the deployed commit after the fix.\ncounter: No unrelated staging service is restarted or redeployed during diagnosis.\nevidence: staging health check\nscope in: remote-dev boot path, staging health signal, GitHub and AWS evidence\nscope out: production deploys, unrelated ECS services, broad infra refactors\nunknowns: current deploy commit, service health signal\nconfidence gaps: current deploy commit, cloud credential scope\nsummary review: Plan is approved for staging-only diagnosis with captured rollback evidence before changes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[28.0, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging demo data cleanup\n\nuser role: Product engineer preparing a clean staging demo while avoiding accidental data loss.\nuser prompt: Clean staging data so tomorrow's demo starts fresh.\nquestion type: recommended destructive boundary\nscore target: 10/10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[30.8, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging demo data cleanup - questions\n\n1. data boundary: What data boundary is allowed for cleanup?\n   user: Only the staging demo company and its generated task executions; never shared seed users.\n2. backup requirement: What proof is required before any destructive command?\n   user: Produce a dry-run deletion report and export IDs before requesting approval.\n3. demo seed source: How should the demo data be recreated?\n   user: Use the existing idempotent demo seed script and verify counts after reseed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[33.6, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Staging demo data cleanup - plan proof\n\nscenario: risky-destructive-action\nscore: 10/10\ntools: read_repo_instructions, git_status, ask_before_destructive_action, targeted_tests,\nno_mutation_in_plan_mode\nsuccess: Dry-run report matches the approved demo-company boundary before any delete runs.\ncounter: Shared seed users and non-demo companies remain untouched after reseed verification.\nevidence: dry-run deletion report\nscope in: dry-run deletion report, approval gate, idempotent reseed verification\nscope out: production data, shared seed users, manual SQL delete without preview\nunknowns: destructive scope, reseed path\nconfidence gaps: destructive scope, repeatable reseed path\nsummary review: Plan is approved only up to dry-run evidence; destructive execution requires a separate\napproval.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[36.4, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Flaky UI library issue\n\nuser role: Frontend engineer debugging a browser-specific select dropdown issue.\nuser prompt: The new dropdown sometimes closes immediately in Safari. Figure out whether we need docs,\nbrowser testing, or both.\nquestion type: multi-question flow\nscore target: 10/10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[39.2, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Flaky UI library issue - questions\n\n1. library name: Which UI library owns the dropdown behavior?\n   user: It is Radix Select via @radix-ui/react-select.\n2. installed version: Should the plan discover the installed version before reading docs?\n   user: Yes, inspect package files first and only then fetch version-matched docs.\n3. browser symptom: What browser behavior should be reproduced?\n   user: Safari closes the select right after open when the trigger is inside a modal.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[42.0, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Flaky UI library issue - plan proof\n\nscenario: tool-choice-ambiguity\nscore: 10/10\ntools: read_repo_instructions, git_status, context7_docs, browser_qa, targeted_tests,\nno_mutation_in_plan_mode\nsuccess: Safari reproduction is captured and the fix cites version-matched Radix Select docs.\ncounter: Chromium behavior remains unchanged in the same Playwright scenario.\nevidence: doc citation and screenshot\nscope in: package version discovery, Context7 docs, Safari and Chromium browser QA\nscope out: rewriting the design system select primitive without reproduction, AWS or staging checks\nunknowns: library version, browser reproduction\nconfidence gaps: library version, browser reproduction\nsummary review: Plan is approved around package discovery first, then docs plus browser reproduction.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
[44.8, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H================================================================================================================\n Simulation Result\n\nsessions passed: 5/5\naggregate score: 50/50\nartifact source: merak-plan-user-sim-report.json\nthis proves the benchmarked behavior, not general model omniscience.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n================================================================================================================"]
